{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035707-diamond-vs-free-council-vs-seers-of-the-throne","id":1035707,"title":"Diamond Vs Free Council vs Seers of the Throne","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-21T07:42:43-08:00","id":1035707,"title":"Diamond Vs Free Council vs Seers of the Throne","content":"I am looking for more information on the Political differences for the Various Sects.<br /> <br /> The Diamond Orders are made up of the Adamantine Arrow, Guardians of the Veil, The Mysterium, and the Silver Ladder.<br /> The Diamond Orders and the Free Council make up the Pentacle.<br /> The Pentacle stand against the Seers of the Throne.<br /> <br /> <b>Concilium:</b> The individual orders in the Diamond Order are governed by Caucuses and have representatives in the local Concilia. The Diamond Orders form a Concilium to govern an area. Each Concilium sends representatives to the Convocation. The Diamond Orders follow the Laws set forth in the Lex Magica. <span style=\"color:blue\">Do they have a Court system and if so what is the Court Structure of the Concilia? Is it a panel of Judges, a judge and a jury, monarchy?</span><br /> <br /> <b>Roles:</b><br /> Hierarch<br /> Councilor<br /> Provost<br /> Sentinel<br /> Herald<br /> Interfector<br /> <br /> <b>Lex Magics (Laws)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Gold Laws:</b> Order Wide<br /> Individual Studies.<br /> Maintain Sencta/Hollows without trespass.<br /> Recognized for greater skill in the Arcana.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Laws:</b><br /> Local Laws (Could stretch to the whole Convocation)<br /> The Precept of Secrecy<br /> The Precept of Protectorate<br /> The Precept of Hubris<br /> The Precept of War<br /> <br /> <b>Bronze Laws:</b><br /> Strictly Local Laws<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Laws:</b><br /> Rules, oaths, and treaties ratified by a small group of mages within the Consilium\u2019s jurisdiction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Free Council</b> The free council is an order and a sect. I know that where there are few members of the Free Council they agree to follow the laws and governing of the local Concilium. <span style=\"color:blue\">Do they have an equivalent to the Lex Magica, or do they adopt the Lex Magica as their laws? If they have their own laws is it structured the same gold, silver, bronze and iron?</span><br /> <br /> <b>Roles:</b><br /> Voter<br /> Host<br /> Emissaries<br /> Minutemen<br /> Letter Carriers<br /> Citizen Agents<br /> Strategos<br /> Syndic<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Seers of the Throne</b> I am assuming that they have Ministry laws, Tetrarchy laws and Pylon laws. There courts are informal and is handled by the local authority, usually the highest ranked Pylon in the area.<br /> <br /> <b>Roles:</b><br /> Ministers<br /> Tetrarchs<br /> Pylons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-21-2017, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T08:12:57-08:00","id":1035713,"title":"","content":"Though it's pretty early 1e, Sanctum and Sigil still has lots and lots of information on how a consilia functions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:blue\">Do they have an equivalent to the Lex Magica, or do they adopt the Lex Magica as their laws?</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They don't seem to, though I don't remember it ever being directly addressed. They presumably have constitutional structures that determine how their assmblies work, but it seems implied that most things are done on the basis of direct democracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Seers of the Throne</b> I am assuming that they have Ministry laws, Tetrarchy laws and Pylon laws. There courts are informal and is handled by the local authority, usually the highest ranked Pylon in the area. </div> </div> </div>It's basically Fuhrerprinzip. You do what you're told by your superiors and try and get away with what you can. There's no court system, you're always someone elses subordinate and they tell you what to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T08:28:19-08:00","id":1035714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035707-diamond-vs-free-council-vs-seers-of-the-throne#post1035707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The individual orders in the Diamond Order are governed by Caucuses and have representatives in the local Concilia.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a possibly accurate statement, in that members of each Order will be represented in the Consilium's membership (that is, the Consilium's membership will be made up of members who can theoretically belong to any Order represented in the region), but there isn't a requirement of each Consilium having a formal representative from each Order. Most Hierarchs will be canny enough to try and stack their Councilors with representatives from the Pentacle but that's not always the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035707-diamond-vs-free-council-vs-seers-of-the-throne#post1035707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Diamond Orders form a Concilium to govern an area. Each Concilium sends representatives to the Convocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consiliums are more of a cabal thing; a given cabal and its allies declaring a Consilium in the region, rather than a given Order. Each Consilium will send representatives to a Convocation as well, though, depending on circumstances, other groups may also try and send representatives to speak on a particular issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035707-diamond-vs-free-council-vs-seers-of-the-throne#post1035707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Diamond Orders follow the Laws set forth in the Lex Magica. <span style=\"color:blue\">Do they have a Court system and if so what is the Court Structure of the Concilia? Is it a panel of Judges, a judge and a jury, monarchy?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The Lex Magicka is the name for the laws that govern the Awakened, but there is no singular set of laws. The Gold Laws are the ones that are pretty much universal; incorporated into just about every Consilium. The rest, as you note, are more local affairs.<br /> <br /> As for whether they have a court system... The Consilia <i>is</i> the court system; that is its entire raison d'etre; to regulate the interactions of the Awakened. While different regions may have different patterns of justice and trial, the usual path is that any case brought before the Consilium and found to have merit is argued before the Councilors or Hierarch or both, with the accuser and accused both having to make their own cases. The judging party may then require another group to perform an independent investigation and then decides on the result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035707-diamond-vs-free-council-vs-seers-of-the-throne#post1035707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Free Council</b> The free council is an order and a sect. I know that where there are few members of the Free Council they agree to follow the laws and governing of the local Concilium. <span style=\"color:blue\">Do they have an equivalent to the Lex Magica, or do they adopt the Lex Magica as their laws? If they have their own laws is it structured the same gold, silver, bronze and iron?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The Free Council has no particularly formal structure. When Assemblies do form, they likely vote on a charter or constitution to which all members must attest, and that founding document probably resembles the standard formula of the Lex Magicka. The Lex didn't just manifest <i>ex nihilo</i>; it covers a lot of rules the Awakened cleave to for a reason. That said, in the developed world, it's hard not to picture these foundational documents resembling a constitution; the influence of the Enlightenment (and, more pointedly, the United States) is too strong. They probably enumerate the rights of members, then add laws on top of that which may need to change with time. Beyond that, there's probably no structuring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1035707-diamond-vs-free-council-vs-seers-of-the-throne#post1035707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Seers of the Throne</b> I am assuming that they have Ministry laws, Tetrarchy laws and Pylon laws. There courts are informal and is handled by the local authority, usually the highest ranked Pylon in the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Seers don't really need laws; they have edicts. Whomever is in charge says what the rules are and everyone either obeys or usurps them. There isn't really a need for anything beyond that. If a Seer does feel the need to lay down the rules for those beneath them, they might do so via a formal decree and possibly appoint someone in their Pylon (or other hierarchy) to watch out for violations, but there isn't really a need to go any further.<br /> <br /> The Seers aren't interested in justice or moral order for the most part. They're interested in obedience. A tyrant is absolute and not restricted by the rule of law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T08:40:23-08:00","id":1035717,"title":"","content":"Thank you both <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar178_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"178\" data-vbnamecard=\"178\">Michael</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> I appreciate the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}